<% content_for(:title, "Terminal - Asterism Console") %>
<% content_for(:head) do %>
  <%= stylesheet_link_tag("xterm", "data-turbo-track": "reload") %>
  <%# Its own content security policy (TerminalsController): never swapped in by Turbo. %>
  <meta name="turbo-visit-control" content="reload">
<% end %>
<div class="console terminal-page" data-controller="terminal"
     data-terminal-available-value="<%= @available %>"
     data-terminal-user-value="<%= current_user.id %>"
     data-terminal-level-value="<%= current_user.rshell_access %>"
     data-terminal-file-max-value="<%= TerminalFiles::FILE_MAX %>">
  <header class="bar">
    <h1><%= link_to "Asterism Console", root_path, data: { turbo: false } %></h1>
    <span class="hint">Terminal</span>
    <%= render "shared/nav" %>
  </header>

  <%# One line by default; the rest under More (docs/terminal.md). %>
  <nav class="layers terminal-help" aria-label="About the Terminal">
    <span class="hint terminal-tips"><code>help</code> lists the commands. Tab completes, &uarr;&darr; the history,
      Ctrl-C stops.</span>
    <button type="button" class="link-button terminal-more-toggle" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="terminal-more"
            data-terminal-target="moreToggle" data-action="terminal#toggleMore">More</button>
    <span class="terminal-where" data-terminal-target="where" hidden></span>
    <span class="counts" data-terminal-target="state" role="status"></span>
  </nav>
  <div class="terminal-more hint" id="terminal-more" data-terminal-target="more" hidden>
    <p>The asterism command line's commands, run by the console on its connection (<code>help</code> lists them).
      Reading is open to everyone signed in; <code>call</code> runs only the methods an admin allowed under Call
      permissions. Every command is kept in the <%= link_to "Call log", calls_path(anchor: "terminal") %>.</p>
    <p>Tab completes, &uarr;&darr; the history, Ctrl-C stops, Ctrl-L clears the screen.</p>
    <p><code>remote &lt;node&gt;</code> goes into a machine (the remote shell, for the users an admin allowed under
      Users; <code>remote</code> lists the machines), <code>exit</code> or Ctrl-D leaves it. In a machine,
      <code>get &lt;file&gt;</code> brings a file to this browser and <code>put [&lt;folder&gt;]</code> (or files
      dropped on the Terminal) writes files there.</p>
  </div>

  <main class="body terminal-body">
    <div class="terminal-frame">
      <div class="terminal-wrap" data-terminal-target="screen" aria-label="Terminal"></div>
    </div>
  </main>
</div>
